# Performance — budgets & profiling

## Frame loop law
- **60 FPS target** on the reference laptop you name in `docs/renderer-info.md`
- Name the device class for any mobile reading you report

## Budgets (course caps — tighten per route)
- **Draw calls (full scene):** ≤ 200 on desktop, ≤ 80 on mobile — the safety rail
- **Your accepted ceiling:** the measured row for your tree, written in `src/budget.js` (`CEILING`) and `docs/renderer-info.md` in the same PR
- **Textures:** `renderer.info.memory.textures` is a COUNT, not bytes (1 with every map null — three's placeholder). GPU bytes are computed, as the KTX2 satellite teaches
- **Shadows:** off by default; a shadow map doubles calls and adds textures — only with a before/after row

## Post-processing
- Zero passes is the reference. One pass only with comparable renderer readings before and after (Unit 9's per-frame probe)

## Profiling workflow
- Read the gallery panel (the shared `BudgetProbe`, ~1 Hz, previous frame) on your own route and machine
- Chrome Performance panel for frame time when the panel is not enough
- Change the tree → change `CEILING` and the renderer-info row together

## Anti-patterns
- Copying another tree's numbers (the beacon's 6 / 1368) into your row
- `setState` at frame rate; allocation inside `useFrame`
- Full-screen transparent quads; per-object real-time shadows
